SUMMARY:Volunteer Opportunity: West Virginia Robotics Extreme (WVRoX) – 2-day endurance robotics competition
DESCRIPTION:Fairmont State University's SciTech Education Resource Center\, in coordination with Mountaineer Area RoboticS FIRST Robotics Competition (FRC) team 2614\, is hosting the semi-annual WVRoX endurance robotics competition. This one-of-a-kind event features 30 FRC teams from across the nation competing through the night in a test of ingenuity and endurance. As you can imagine\, a large number of volunteers are needed to make this event happen. Volunteers serve in 4-hour shifts in a variety of roles\, including roles for which no prior experience in robotics is necessary. More information about WVRoX\, including a volunteer signup link\, is available athttps://www.marsfirst.org/wvrox.
LOCATION:Fairmont State University Falcon Center
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/030c7daa-9dc4-432a-9ccb-6d9b145ba30741b00ae5-3c52-432e-8676-278d5c34d9ab.png
END:VEVENT
